WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:03.880
When the coronavirus pandemic forced
much of the world into lockdown,

00:00:03.960 --> 00:00:07.360
it highlighted what social creatures
we humans are.

00:00:07.720 --> 00:00:10.760
More than half of UK adults surveyed
agreed that a reduction

00:00:10.840 --> 00:00:14.040
in social contact during lockdown
made life harder.

00:00:14.120 --> 00:00:16.480
Social neuroscientist John Cacioppo

00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:19.480
argued that: "loneliness
is an evolutionary signal

00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:22.800
telling us something is not right
with your social environment,

00:00:22.880 --> 00:00:26.000
and that you need to do
something about it, fast".

00:00:26.080 --> 00:00:28.360
Having really good relationships
in your life

00:00:28.440 --> 00:00:31.480
is fundamental
to your personal well-being.

00:00:31.560 --> 00:00:36.000
And being able to reach out to people
who really care about you

00:00:36.080 --> 00:00:37.440
is so important.

00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:40.200
So why does maintaining
friendships and relationships

00:00:40.280 --> 00:00:42.320
sometimes feel so hard?

00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:45.400
We can all strengthen the
relationships we have in our lives

00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:47.680
as well as creating quality new ones.

00:00:47.760 --> 00:00:50.920
Here are some tips to help you
connect better with those around you.

00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:56.080
The first one is listen.

00:00:56.160 --> 00:00:59.200
It's all very well being interesting,

00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:03.240
but it's equally important to be
interested in what other people

00:01:03.320 --> 00:01:04.840
have got to say to you.

00:01:04.920 --> 00:01:08.840
So really listening helps people
to feel more valued.

00:01:08.920 --> 00:01:11.080
Active listening is a skill,

00:01:11.160 --> 00:01:13.240
one we can all practise
and get better at.

00:01:13.680 --> 00:01:16.320
When you're in a conversation,
non-verbal signs

00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:20.160
such as eye contact, mirroring
and nodding all help create

00:01:20.240 --> 00:01:21.760
a positive environment.

00:01:22.360 --> 00:01:24.360
Asking questions for clarification

00:01:24.440 --> 00:01:27.040
and paraphrasing and
reflecting back what is said

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:30.560
also shows that you're really trying
to understand what someone is saying.

00:01:31.320 --> 00:01:33.920
Being an active listener
means that you recognise

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:37.280
the conversation is more about
the other person than about you.

00:01:38.680 --> 00:01:42.320
Sometimes you can feel lonely even
though there are people around you.

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:46.280
Making sure that the time you spend
with other people is of good quality

00:01:46.360 --> 00:01:48.200
can help combat those feelings.

00:01:48.480 --> 00:01:52.040
Switch off the television,
play some games, cook together,

00:01:52.120 --> 00:01:56.440
communicate, really talk to each
other, and spend that time together.

00:01:56.920 --> 00:01:59.160
Whether we feel happy and
connected with our loved ones

00:01:59.240 --> 00:02:01.640
may depend on the activities
we do together.

00:02:02.280 --> 00:02:05.120
One study found that our happiness
and feelings of closeness

00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:07.600
are more to do with
different types of activities

00:02:07.680 --> 00:02:09.760
we do with friends
and family members

00:02:09.840 --> 00:02:12.080
as opposed to the
relationships themselves.

00:02:12.800 --> 00:02:16.120
One distraction that often gets in
the way is your mobile phone.

00:02:16.200 --> 00:02:19.080
Very often we can be in
conversation with people

00:02:19.160 --> 00:02:21.360
and we're not absolutely present.

00:02:21.440 --> 00:02:25.280
So putting the mobile technology
away is a really good way

00:02:25.360 --> 00:02:26.600
to create that connection.

00:02:27.600 --> 00:02:30.480
Another skill that can help
is talking openly.

00:02:31.160 --> 00:02:33.160
Author Susan Scott wrote:

00:02:33.240 --> 00:02:36.040
"Never be afraid of the
conversations you're having.

00:02:36.120 --> 00:02:38.920
Be afraid of the conversations
you're not having".

00:02:39.240 --> 00:02:42.360
If there's things that you
feel frustrated about

00:02:42.440 --> 00:02:43.920
and you need to get off your chest,

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:48.640
it's a really good idea to talk about
them rather than let them fester.

00:02:49.080 --> 00:02:50.600
Often we might not want to talk

00:02:50.680 --> 00:02:53.440
because we are afraid we might
upset the other person

00:02:53.520 --> 00:02:55.280
or damage our relationship with them,

00:02:55.720 --> 00:02:58.960
and sometimes we just don't know
how to raise an issue skilfully.

00:02:59.560 --> 00:03:03.160
So firstly, ask yourself: "What's
really bothering me?"

00:03:03.760 --> 00:03:06.360
You can bring it up in an open
and respectful way

00:03:06.920 --> 00:03:09.560
with phrases like:
"I have a concern"

00:03:09.640 --> 00:03:11.920
or: "This is how I feel when...".

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:13.600
Listen to the other person's thoughts

00:03:13.680 --> 00:03:16.600
and genuinely try to understand
where they are coming from.

00:03:16.680 --> 00:03:19.680
Asking: "I am curious
to understand why...",

00:03:19.760 --> 00:03:22.920
or: "Why do you say this?"
can really help with that.

00:03:23.000 --> 00:03:27.040
And don't forget to tell people
how much you care about them,

00:03:27.120 --> 00:03:30.560
how important they are to you,
and how much you value them.

00:03:30.640 --> 00:03:32.840
It's also important to bear in mind

00:03:32.920 --> 00:03:35.760
that you are never going
to change anybody,

00:03:35.840 --> 00:03:39.280
but the only person that you
can really change is yourself.

00:03:39.360 --> 00:03:43.720
So sometimes, rather than focusing
on all the things that irritate you

00:03:43.800 --> 00:03:47.880
about somebody, it's important
to focus on their strengths.

00:03:48.320 --> 00:03:51.000
Another thing that can help
you really connect with others

00:03:51.080 --> 00:03:52.200
is kindness.

00:03:52.520 --> 00:03:54.560
Studies have found that
being kind to others

00:03:54.640 --> 00:03:56.400
is linked to increased
feelings of happiness,

00:03:56.480 --> 00:03:58.640
well-being, and life satisfaction.

00:03:59.720 --> 00:04:01.880
It doesn't need to be grand gestures,

00:04:01.960 --> 00:04:05.280
sometimes it can be the little things
that really make a difference.

00:04:05.360 --> 00:04:08.640
Acknowledging somebody,
giving them eye contact, smiling,

00:04:08.720 --> 00:04:11.320
opening a door, perhaps
picking up some litter

00:04:11.400 --> 00:04:14.440
or making an environment
more comfortable for somebody,

00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:19.000
or a compliment, can really help
to make a person's day glow.

00:04:19.480 --> 00:04:22.720
There are many reasons why kindness
might have this positive effect.

00:04:23.200 --> 00:04:24.240
It can boost our mood,

00:04:24.320 --> 00:04:27.080
and acts of kindness can
help us feel more capable.

00:04:27.160 --> 00:04:28.480
There is also some evidence

00:04:28.560 --> 00:04:31.200
that it can help us buffer the
negative effects of stress.

00:04:31.840 --> 00:04:34.960
Kindness is thought to be one
of the key ways that people create,

00:04:35.040 --> 00:04:37.880
maintain, and strengthen
their social connections.

00:04:38.720 --> 00:04:42.680
We're living in a world where we're
more connected than we've ever been.

00:04:42.760 --> 00:04:45.520
But really positive connections
aren't just about

00:04:45.600 --> 00:04:48.240
people who like you
on the internet,

00:04:48.320 --> 00:04:52.120
it's about people who are going
to be with you for the good times

00:04:52.200 --> 00:04:53.520
and for the bad times.

00:04:53.600 --> 00:04:55.840
Making great connections in your life

00:04:55.920 --> 00:04:58.800
is a little bit like building
sturdy bridges,

00:04:58.880 --> 00:05:01.880
because they can help
to transport you safely

00:05:01.960 --> 00:05:04.040
through challenging times
in your life.

